  "solution": {
    "text": "Given : Radius of hydrogen atom $=0.530$<br />$Å$, Number of excited state $(n)=2$ and atomic number of hydrogen atom $(Z)=1$. We know that the Bohr radius<br />$(r)=\\frac{n^2}{Z} \\times \\text { radius of atom }=\\frac{(2)^2}{1} \\times 0.530$<br />$=4 \\times 0.530=2.12 Å$",
    "image": null
